    "title": "Springfield teen seriously injured in Polk County wreck - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kathryn Skopec ,\n1 hours ago\nPOLK COUNTY, Mo. — An 18-year-old Springfield woman suffered serious injuries in a single-vehicle crash Wednesday evening north of Greene County.\nAccording to a Missouri State Highway Patrol (MSHP) crash report, the wreck occurred at 6:34 p.m. on Route H, about one mile south of Pleasant Hope, in Polk County.\nTroopers said the teen was driving a southbound 2015 Chrysler 200 when she failed to negotiate a curve, went off the right side of the road, struck a driveway, became airborne, overturned and hit a tree.\nShe was taken to Cox Medical Center South in Springfield by Citizens Memorial Hospital EMS. She was wearing a seat belt, according to the report.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KOLR - OzarksFirst.com.",
